<h1 id="summary">Summary</h1>

<p>Because my spare time is limited, I couldn’t manage to post two articles a month steadily. I hope everyone understands. The Douyin animation series requires writing a demo first and then studying it carefully before turning it into an article. It takes real effort to make. This article also references open-source code and some scrolling-caption libraries. Since the demo isn’t perfect, some classes still have room for extension — for example, exposing the start/end animation to the outside, or naturally adding an animation group like the system does. This article thanks the open-source author <a href="https://github.com/sshiqiao/douyin-ios-objectc">qiaoshi</a>, because the author’s implementation wasn’t perfect, so I studied it and added gradient effects and attributed string support.</p>

